hadiths[164]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1658","Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather, \A long time passed that we did not pray any more than five prayers.\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us and we gathered together. The narrator (i.e. Ubaidullah) Muhammad bin Ubaidullah Azim is weak."""
"1659","Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to perform three rak'ahs of Witrada, in which he used to recite Surah Al-Ala, Surah Al-Kafrun and Surah Al-Ikhlas. used to do"
"1660","Sayyiduna Abi Ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Surah Al-Ala, Surah Al-Kafrun, Surah Al-Ikhlas in the three rak'ats of Witr, and before going into Ruku, he recited the Qunoot Dua."
"1661","Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Surah Al-Ala, Surah Al-Kafrun and Surah Al-Ikhlas during the Witr prayer."
"1662","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) narrates that one night I stayed with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in order to find out when the Qunut prayer is recited in the Witr prayer. How do I pray Qunut? So my mother came and told me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Qunut before bowing."
"1663","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Qunut before bowing in the Witr prayer."
"1664","Sayyidna Suwayd bin Ghafla (RA) narrates, I have heard Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar, Sayyidna Uthman, Sayyidna Ali (RA) narrating that the Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Qunut at the end of Witr. These Companions also used to do the same."
"1665","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to not return salam after performing two rak'ahs of witr."
"1666","Muhammad bin Sirin narrates that I asked Sayyidna Anas bin Malik about the Dua of Qunut, and he replied that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the Dua of Qunut after bowing."
"1667","Muhammad bin Sirin narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Anas, may the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite the Qunut supplication in the morning prayer. He answered yes! (It has been read) Narrator narrates, then it was asked whether the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the Qunoot supplication in the Fajr prayer. So they answered yes! It is recited a little after Ruku."
"1668","Abu Uthman narrates that Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar (RA) used to recite Qunut after Ruku in the morning prayer."
"1669","Qays bin Abu Hazim narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Sa'd (RA) performing one rak'ah after the Isha prayer, so I asked him which prayer it was. So he said, I have seen the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing one rakat and witrada."
"1670","Muhammad bin Abdur Rahman narrates that Sayyidna Saad bin Abi Waqqas (RA) offered the Isha prayer, then performed one rak'ah and then a person asked him, O Abu Ishaq! Didn't I see you performing one rak'ah and witrada? So they inquired, then Sayyidna Saad said, O blind! Will you teach me my religion?"
"1671","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \Will you teach me the method of my prayer?\"""""
"1672","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to perform one rak'ah and witrada."
"1673","Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman narrates that once I thought that tonight no place would be able to separate me from Ibrahim. A man came and placed his hand between my shoulders. You performed one rak'ah, so they replied that it was my witr."
"1674","Ibn Abi Malikah narrates that a person said to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him: \Do you not wonder about Sayyidna Mu'awiya"," may God be pleased with him"," who prays one rak'ah and Witrada?\"" Then Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas"," may God be pleased with him"," said"," \""Yes"," he is a jurist.\"""""
"1675","Syed Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the first rak'ah of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) was the second rak'ah of Witr, in which he used to recite Surah Al-Ala and Surah Al-Kafrun and then in the witr rak'at he recited Surah Al-Ikhlas, Surah Al-Falaq and Surah Al-Nas."
"1676","Syed Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform three rak'ahs of witrada."
"1677","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person asked the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Witr."
"1678","The same hadith has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him, along with another chain of transmission."
"1679","Salim narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the Anfal on his ride, regardless of the direction it was facing, he used to perform the Witr on him, but he did not perform the obligatory prayer while riding."
"1680","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to perform the Witr prayer on his horse."
"1681","The freed slave of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, Sayyidna Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that once we were on a journey with the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace."
"1682","Sayyida Umm Salma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform a short rak'at after Witr."
"1683","The freed slave of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, Sayyidna Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: We were on a journey with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: \Travel causes trouble and fatigue"," so when a person performs Witrah"," then he should perform two rak'ahs after that. If he wakes up"," then it is fine"," otherwise these two rak'ahs will be enough for him.\"""""
"1684","Sayyidna Bara (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Qunut in the Fajr and Maghrib prayers. The narrator Abu Bakr Naami has narrated this."
"1685","Sayyidna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Qunut in the morning and evening prayers."
"1686","Muhammad bin Sirin narrated this hadith to me by the person who had performed the Fajr prayer following the example of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head after the second rak'ah and stood for a while (i.e. during which he recited the Qunut prayer)."
"1687","Sayyidna Bara bin Azib (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Qunut in whatever duty he performed."
"1688","Abdullah bin Nafi' narrated this statement of Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) regarding his father. The narrators of this hadith, Muhammad bin Yala, Anbasa, Abdullah bin Nafi, are all weak, and it is not proven that another narrator, Nafi, heard the hadith from Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA)."
"1689","This same tradition along with another chain of transmission is related to Safia bint Abu Ubayd from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but this woman named Safia was not blessed with the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1690","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) went into Ruku during the prayer, then he raised his head and said this dua. O Allah! Save Ayyash bin Rabia! O Allah! Save Salma bin Hisham! O Allah! Give salvation to Waleed bin Waleed! O Allah! Save the weak Muslims! O Allah! Send down your harshness harmful (on the members of the tribe)! O Allah! In the time of Syedna Yusuf (peace be upon him), impose a famine on them! (O Allah!) Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went into prostration."
"1691","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates, \I pray in a better way than all of you according to the way of the Prophet (PBUH).\"" The narrator narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may God be pleased with him) in the last rak'ah of the Zuhr 'Isha prayer"," \""after reading Sama'Allah Liman Hamda"," he used to recite Qunut and pray for the believers and curse the disbelievers.\"""""
"1692","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) continued to recite Qunut in the Fajr prayer until he (PBUH) left this world."
"1693","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Qunut for a month, in which he prayed for harm for them (infidels), then he abandoned it."
"1694","Rabi bin Anas narrates that once I was sitting with Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, and said to him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited Qunut for a month."
"1695","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that I have prayed following the example of the Prophet (PBUH) 'The Prophet (PBUH) kept reciting the Qunut after bowing in the morning prayer until I separated from him. (i.e. he left the world)."
"1696","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I recited Dua Qunut following the example of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) until I separated from them (i.e. they left this world)."
"1697","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar and Sayyidna Uthman (the narrator says 'I think' he also mentioned the fourth Caliph) recited the Dua of Qunut, 'until I separated from them."
"1698","Hasan Basri narrates that Sayyidna Anas (RA) said to me that I recited Dua Qunut following the example of the Prophet (PBUH) and Sayyidna Umar (RA) until I became separated from both of them."
"1699","Abu Tufail narrates this about Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with them) that both of them prayed following the example of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the Qunut supplication in the morning prayer."
"1700","Sayyidna Hasan Basri says, \Whoever forgets to recite Qunut in the morning prayer"," it is necessary to perform Sajdah on him.\"""""
"1701","Saeed bin Abdulaziz says about this person, \Whoever forgets to recite the Qunoot prayer in the morning prayer"," it is necessary to perform prostration on him.\"""""
"1702","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform two rak'ahs after Witr, and he used to perform this rak'ah sitting down. Narrator Abu Bakr-Nami has stated that this is the method which the people of Basra are unique in imitating and the people of Syria have preserved it."
"1703","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) kept reciting Qunut prayers until he left this world."
"1704","Saeed bin Jubayr (RA) narrates, “I bear witness that I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) saying, ‘Reciting Qunut in the morning prayer is an innovation."
"1705","Abu Qalaba says: I met Sayyidna Amr, and he told me this hadith: We used to live in a place where there was water and it was a passage for people. Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I kept remembering that word and it became firm in my heart. The common Arabs suspended their acceptance of Islam with the conquest of Makkah. They used to say that this Prophet and his people should be justified. If he prevails over his people, then he will be a true prophet. When we received the news of the conquest of Makkah, every nation hurried to accept Islam. He stayed with the Holy Prophet for some time. When he returned from serving the Holy Prophet, we went to meet him. When he saw us, he swore by Allah! I am coming to you from the true Messenger of Allah. He has ordered you to do this. He has said that this is how you should pray at this time. This is how you should pray at this time. This is how you should pray at this time. I was made to stand in front 'I was 6 or 7 years old at that time' 'I had a cloak which was small' I used to go to Sajdah and it was removed, so a woman of the tribe said: Why don't you people cover the back part of your Qari? Then the tribesmen gave me a shirt which was made of Bahraini cloth."
"1706","Imam Jafar Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) quotes his father (Imam Baqir) on Imam Zain al-Abidin (may Allah have mercy on him) on the authority of Imam Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). If the sick person is able to pray standing, then he should pray standing, otherwise he should pray sitting. He should pray and both his feet should be in the direction of Qiblah."
"1707","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma narrates that a sick person should pray with his feet facing the Qibla while lying on the mat."
"1708","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a person is praying and he vomits, he should put his hand over his mouth and ask someone who is the best among those present to lead him. If it has not been done, then he will pray anew."
"1709","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Sunnah is that a person should not go out (to pray the Eid prayer) until he has taken some food and paid Sadaqah al-Fitr."
"1710","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that (a person) should not go out on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr until he has taken some food and given Sadaqah al-Fitr."
"1711","Hanash bin Mu'tamarbayan narrates, \I saw Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) on the day of Eid-ul-Adha. He kept reciting Takbeer until he reached the Eidgah.\"""""
"1712","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to leave the mosque to pray the Eid prayer and would continue to recite the Takbeer until he reached the Eidgah and would continue to recite the Takbeer until the Imam came."
"1713","Abu Abd al-Rahman Salmi narrates that in earlier times, people used to recite Takbeer on Eid-ul-Fitr with greater intensity (i.e. louder) than on Eid-ul-Adha."
"1714","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to leave his house on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr and start reciting Takbeer until he (PBUH) used to come to the Eidgah."
"1715","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Buraidah (RA) narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (PBUH) did not go out (to pray) on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr until he had eaten something, and he (PBUH) did not eat anything on the day of Eid-ul-Adha until he returned (after performing the Eid prayer) then he used to eat the meat of the sacrifice. Abdul Samadnami the narrator has quoted these words until he used to sacrifice."
"1716","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that 'when he would leave on the day of Eid al-Ladha or the day of Eid al-Fitr, he would recite the takbeer continuously until he reached the place of Eid."
"1717","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not go out on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr until he ate some dates."
"1718","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not go out (to pray) on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr until he had eaten some dates."
"1719","Ubaydullah bin Abdullah narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) asked Sayyidna Abu Waqid Laithi (RA) which surah the Prophet (PBUH) used to recite in the Eid-ul-Fitr prayer and in the Eid-ul-Zhaha prayer. So he replied: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Surah Q and Surah Uqtarbat."
"1720","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited twelve takbeers in addition to the initial takbeer in the prayers of both Eids."
"1721","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say seven takbirs in the first rak'at of the Eid prayer and five takbirs in the second rak'at."
"1722","The same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) about the Holy Prophet (PBUH)."
"1723","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) said, 'Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar (RA) used to perform the Eid prayer before giving the sermon."
"1724","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, “On the day of Eid, I participated in the prayer following the example of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1725","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform any prayer before this prayer and after this prayer (the narrator narrates), i.e. the Eid prayer."
"1726","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say seven and five takbeers in the prayers of Eid-ul-Fitr and Eid-ul-Zuha. These words are from the narration of Abu Tahirnami narrator."
"1727","Abdullah bin Muhammad narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say seven takbirs in the first rakat of the Eid prayer, and in the second rakat, he said five takbirs: He used to pray before giving the sermon."
"1728","Amro bin Shoaib, regarding his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said twelve takbirs in the prayer of both Eids, that is, in the prayer of Eid al-Zuha and in the prayer of Eid al-Fitr: He used to say seven takbirs in the first rakat and five takbirs in the second rakat."
"1729","Along with another chain of transmission, it has been narrated about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that seven takbirs will be recited in the first rakat and five takbirs will be recited in the second rakat and the recitation in both rakats will be after these takbirs."
"1730","Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement on the authority of his father, \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited seven takbirs in the first rak'at on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr and five takbirs in the second rak'at.\"" These were in addition to the takbirs of the prayer."""
"1731","Kathir bin Abdullah narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say takbirs in the Eid prayer: He used to say seven takbirs in the first rak'at and five takbirs in the second rak'at. Bukhari quoted these words additionally in his tradition. Before reciting (used to say takbirs)."
"1732","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said that Takbirs will be recited during the Eids."
"1733","Abu Tufail, Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib and Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir, may Allah be pleased with them, narrate this that they cursed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to recite Bismillah along with Surah Al-Fatiha in the obligatory prayer, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the dua of Qunut in the Fajr prayer and in the Witr prayer, and he used to recite the Dua of Qunut in the Fajr prayer and in the Witr prayer, and during the days of Tashreeq, from the beginning of the Fajr prayer on the day of Arafah to the days of Tashreeq. On the last day till Asr prayer, on which day people leave in large numbers, they recite Takbeer after every fard prayer."
"1734","Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim in a loud voice in the obligatory prayer."
"1735","Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of Imam Zain al-Abidin (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the Takbeer after the Fajr prayer on the day of Arafah and continued to recite it until the Asr prayer on the last day of Tashreeq."
"1736","Imam Muhammad Al-Bas Qar (RA) narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) used to say Takbeer on the day of Arafah and he used to finish this act on the last day of ``Tashreeq''."
"1737","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) offered the morning prayer on the day of Arafah, he (PBUH) turned to his companions and said, “Stay in your place.” Then he (PBUH) started reciting this. \Allah is the greatest"," Allah is the greatest"," Allah is the greatest"," Allah is the greatest"," There is no god but Allah"," Allah is the greatest"," Allah is the greatest"," All praise is for Allah.\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to start reciting this takbeer in the morning on the day of Arafah and continued reciting it (after every prayer) until Asr prayer on the last day of Tashreeq."""
"1738","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Sa'ib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was participating in the Eid prayer following the example of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said, \Now we will give the sermon to whoever wants to sit down (the narrator narrates means to sit down to listen to the sermon) and whoever wants to go"," let him go.\"""""
"1739","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the takbeer of the days of Tashreeq will begin after noon on the day of sacrifice and it will be recited for the last time in the morning prayer on the last day of the days of Tashreeq."
"1740","The previous hadith has been narrated from two different sources."
"1741","Narrated by Abdul Malik bin Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi Farah (Abu Marwan), on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Farah, on the authority of Abu Salama Al-Hazrami, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1742","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): People (i.e. the Companions) used to say Takbeer after Zuhr prayer on the Day of Sacrifice and they used to say Takbeer until Zuhr prayer on the last day of Tashreeq."
"1743","A narrator named Abdullah narrates this on the authority of his father, when Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) was confined, he started saying Takbeer in front of us on the Day of Sacrifice from the Zuhr prayer, and he recited the Takbeer until the Zuhr prayer on the last day of ``Tashreeq'' (the last day of ``Tashreeq'')."
"1744","A narrator named Abdullah narrates this about Sayyidna Umar and Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with them. Both of them used to perform Zuhr prayer in Dadi Mohsab on the day of their return and did not say Takbeer after that."
"1745","It has been narrated about Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to say Takbeer after all prayers during the days of Tashreeq: He used to recite Allahu Akbar three times."
"1746","The same hadith has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) along with another chain of transmission."
"1747","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went inside the Kaaba, then he came outside. Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) was behind him. He answered no! The narrator narrates that the next day, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) again went inside the Kaaba. He answered yes! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed two rak'ats. He turned towards the trunk of the tree and placed the second pillar on his right."
"1748","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) entered the Kaaba, and Sayyiduna Bilal (RA) was also with him."
"1749","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went inside the Ka’ba, and he prayed two rak’ahs among his friends. He asked the people and came outside (this time the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not pray inside the Kaaba)."
"1750","Sayyidna Masurabin Mukharama (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Abdullah Ibn Abbas (RA) came to the service of Sayyidna Umar (RA) when he was wounded. He said, Ameerul-Mu'minin, it is time for prayer. Sayyidna Umar (RA) said, \There is no place in Islam for such a person to offer prayer.\"" Then Sayyidna Umar (RA) performed the prayer"," although blood was flowing from his wound at that time."""
"1751","Abdullah bin Burida narrates this statement of his father: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that the main difference between us and them (infidels) is to perform the prayer."
"1752","The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is narrated by Abdullah bin Baridah from his father."
"1753","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: “The main difference between a servant and disbelief is abandoning prayer.”"
"1754","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Kufr (the narrator has doubts, perhaps this is the word) between polytheism and faith (the main difference) is abandoning prayer."
"1755","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \The (main difference) between a servant and a disbeliever is abandoning prayer.\"""""
"1756","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that in the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), there was a person whose worship and austerity we liked very much. We mentioned this person to the Prophet (peace be upon him). At the same time, that person came forward. We said, 'This is that person.' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'You are telling me about a person who has the mark of Satan on his face.' There is no one more virtuous than me and no better than me.' The person replied, 'Allah knows.' I asked Sayyidna Abub! Sayyidna Abu Bakr (peace be upon him) went to him and he was praying. Sayyidna Abu Bakr (peace be upon him) thought this. Shall I kill such a person who is offering Salat?', although the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing those who pray.'"
"1757","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Umar Bin Khattab Radiyallahu Anhu that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to kill those who pray."
"1758","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had henna on both his hands and feet. People said, O Messenger of Allah! It resembles women, so it was ordered that it should be taken out of Madinah and sent to a place called Naqi'. It was said, O Messenger of Allah! Shouldn't we kill him? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am forbidden to kill the worshipers. In one tradition these words are: A eunuch was brought who had henna applied to both his hands and feet."
"1759","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “After me, there will be some rulers over you. A righteous person will be your ruler along with his good deeds and a sinner will be along with his sins. You will get your reward, they will get their sin."
"1760","Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that there are four characteristics that I heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but I did not tell you about them. Today I will tell you about them. Do not make takfir because of the sin of one of my people of the Qiblah, even if he commits a great sin, and offer prayer following the example of every imam, and wage jihad with Haramir (the narrator is doubtful, perhaps these are the words), fight, and the fourth thing is Abu Bakr Sadiq, Umar, Uthman and Ali, and say only good things and say this. \This Ummah has passed away"," they will get the reward for the good deeds they did"," and you will get the reward for the good deeds you do.\"""""
"1761","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Every person who believes that there is no god but Allah"," perform his funeral prayer and pray behind every person who believes that there is no god but Allah.\"""""
"1762","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: perform the funeral prayer for each person, believing in God alone, and pray behind each person, believing in God alone."
"1763","This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA)."
"1764","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this. It is obligatory on you to pray in the lead of every Muslim, whether he is righteous or sinful, even if he commits major sins, and it is obligatory on you to fight with Haramir, whether he is righteous or sinful, even if he commits major sins, and it is obligatory on you to offer the funeral prayer for every Muslim who dies, whether he is righteous or sinful, even if he commits major sins."
"1765","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this. Among the basic teachings of the religion, this is included: \Prayer will be offered behind every good person and sinner"," and Jihad will be fought with Haramir.\"""""
"1766","Sayyiduna Wathila Bin Asqaa (RA) narrates, \The Prophet (PBUH) said: Do not make takfir of your people of the Qiblah"," even if they commit major sins"," and pray in the lead of every Imam"," and participate in Jihad along with Haramir"," and perform the funeral prayer for every deceased.\"" The narrator of this tradition"," Abu Saeed"," is unknown."""
"1767","Sayyidna Wathila bin Asqaa (RA) narrates the same in reference to the Prophet (PBUH), but in it there are these words: \Perform the funeral prayer for every deceased among the people of the Qibla.\"""""
"1768","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Pray behind every righteous person and sinner, perform the funeral prayer of every righteous person and sinner, participate in Jihad with every righteous person and sinner. The narrator named Makhool has not heard the hadiths from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may God be pleased with him) and other than that the narrator is trustworthy."
"1769","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Three things are Sunnah: forming a row behind every imam (praying in congregation), you will get the reward of your prayer, and the burden of his sin will be on him, and taking part in Haramirah Murah Jihad, you will get the reward of your bravery, and his evil will be on him, and performing the funeral prayer for every deceased among the people of Tawheed, even if he committed suicide. The narrator Umar bin Subh is obsolete."
"1770","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that prayer is not performed in fear."
"1771","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up, and the people stood up following his example. When they stood up for the second rak'at, those people who had prostrated with him moved back and they began to protect their brothers. Then another group came and they performed one rak'at with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Everyone was saying Takbeer in the prayer, but they were also protecting each other."
"1772","The same hadith is related to Zahri along with another chain of transmission."
"1773","This tradition is also transmitted along with another document."
"1774","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to perform the prayer of fear. She was close to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the other people stood in their place and protected their brothers. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished prostrating, the back row went into prostration. The row that was near the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) went into prostration, and the others stood up, protecting their brothers."
"1775","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led one group of two groups in the prayer of fear, one group, and the other group stood facing the enemy, then those people retreated and stood facing the enemy instead of their companions, and the other people came forward. Rakaat has been performed."
"1776","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the prayer of fear during a war, and one group stood behind him and another group stood between the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the enemy. The Prophet (PBUH) greeted all of them, then both groups performed one rak'ah later."
"1777","Sayyiduna Abu Ayyash Zarqi narrates that we were with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the place of Isfaan. is more beloved than their children and their own lives, then Sayyiduna Gabriel appeared with this verse in the time between Zuhr and Asr. \And when you are among them"," do not pray.\"" When it was time for prayer"," the people took up their weapons under the command of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When those in the first row prostrated and then stood up"," the people in the back row went into prostration"," then those in the back row took the place of those in the front row"," and those in the front moved in the place of those behind"," then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed"," and all the people bowed with him"," then he raised his head"," and all the people raised their heads. When they sat down"," those in the second row prostrated"," then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) greeted all of them. The narrator says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in this way twice"," once in Isfan and once in the area of Banusalim."""
"1778","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"1779","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besieged Banu Muhareb at the place of Nakhl, then it was announced among the people that the prayer had begun, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the Muslims into two groups. Also perform four rak'ats of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and each group performed four rak'ats."
"1780","Saleh bin Khawat narrates the statement of the Companion who, following the example of the Prophet, offered the prayer of fear in the Battle of Zaat al-Raqqa (the Companions narrate) One group formed a line with the Prophet, and the other group remained in front of the enemy. Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lead them the remaining rak'ah of his prayer, then they remained seated and the group completed their prayer, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon them) greeted them all. Ibn Mahdi says that Imam Malik has issued a fatwa according to this tradition. Ibn Wahhib says that Imam Malik first said to me: I like this tradition the most, but then he changed his position and said: The most favorite thing for me is that those people complete their prayers after returning the salam."
"1781","Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) led his companions in fear prayer, he prayed two rak'ahs to some of the companions, and they returned the salam."
"1782","Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) recited durqaat to them in the prayer of fear, then he recited durqaat to other people and greeted them."
"1783","Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led the people in Maghrib prayer three rak'ahs, then he finished the prayer, then other people came and he also led them three rak'ahs."
"1784","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the prayer of fear. After completing the prayer, they returned the salam, then these people went and stood in the place of the first people, facing the enemy."
"1785","Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) narrates that she asked the Prophet (PBUH) whether a woman can pray only in a shirt and a chador while wearing an apron. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If his shirt is so long that it covers both his feet (then it is permissible to do so). The same hadith is also transmitted along with some other isnaads, however, along with these isnaads, it is transmitted as the saying of Sayyida Umm Salama, may Allah be pleased with her."
"1786","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that once the sun was eclipsed, the Prophet (PBUH) ordered a person to announce that the prayer would be performed in congregation. A narrator named Ibn Abi Dawud says that this is a Sunnah and the people of Madinah are unique in quoting it. A narrator named Abd al-Rahman has narrated this regarding Zuhri: \The eclipse prayer should be announced.\"""""
"1787","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"1788","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that once in the blessed life of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the sun was eclipsed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the mosque. He recited Sama’Allah Laman Hamdah Rabbanna Wilk Al-Hamd and then he stood up and started reciting ‘but it was less than the previous recitation’ then after that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed a long bow saying Takbeer ‘but it was less than the first Ruk’ah’ then after that he recited Sama’Allah Laman Hamdah Rabbanna Wilk Al-Hamd’ then he did the same in the second Rak’at and he did it four times in these two Rak’ats. Bowed and prostrated four times. The sun had risen before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer."
"1789","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed the solar eclipse prayer. This hadith is narrated in the same way as it is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Sayyida Aisha that she bowed twice in each rak'at."
"1790","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited long (in the solar eclipse prayer). A narrator named Ibn Abu Dawud narrates that the people of Madinah are unique in imitating reciting aloud."
"1791","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed eight times in four rak'ats in the lunar eclipse and solar eclipse prayers, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in each rak'at."
"1792","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed four times (in two rak'ahs) and prostrated himself four times during the solar eclipse and lunar eclipse prayers."
"1793","Sayyiduna Abu Bakra (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the sun was eclipsed during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). There is also this in this hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said that when Allah Ta’ala manifests on something from His creation, it (bows) before Him with humility and humility."
"1794","Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) said that when Allah Ta'ala manifests for something from among His creatures, it bows before Him. The same tradition is narrated with another document."
"1795","Muhammad bin Ali (may he refer to Imam Muhammad al-Baqir, may Allah be pleased with him) says that there are two signs of our Mahdi that have never occurred after the creation of the heavens and the earth: the eclipse of the moon on the first night of Ramadan and the eclipse of the sun on the fifteenth day of the month when Allah created the heavens and the earth."
"1796","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the sun and the moon are the signs of Allah Almighty."
"1797","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates, “I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying, ‘Once a Prophet went out with the people to perform the Istiqa prayer."
"1798","Imam Jafar Sadiq (RA) narrates this with reference to his father (Imam Muhammad Al-Baqir (RA)): The Prophet (PBUH) used to fold his cloak while praying for rain so that the famine would end."
"1799","Ibad bin Tamim narrates this statement of his uncle: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the Eidgah to pray the Istiqah prayer. A narrator named Sufyan says that while turning the cloak upside down, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned its right side to the left and the left side to the right."
"1800","A narrator named Talha narrates that Marwan sent me to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) so that I could inquire from him about the Sunnah method of performing the Istiqa prayer. Sayyidna Abdullah bin RA said: \Istiqa (i.e."," to pray for rain) is the Sunnah to perform the Istiqa prayer in the Eidgah.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rak'ahs. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the Takbeer seven times in the first rak'ah and recited Surah Al-Ala while in the second rak'ah he recited the Surah Al-Gashiya."""
"1801","Ibad bin Tamim narrates this statement of his uncle: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out with the people to pray for rain."
"1802","Ibad bin Tamim narrates this statement of his uncle: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out with the people to pray for rain. He came to the Eidgah and prayed for rain."
"1803","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to recite aloud during Eid and Istiqa prayers."
"1804","Ubad bin Tamim narrates this statement of his uncle Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to pray for rain. He gave a sermon to the people."
"1805","This same hadith along with some other isnads has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd."
"1806","Ishaq bin Abdullah narrates that Waleed bin Utbah, the governor of Madinah, sent him to Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: O my nephew! You should inquire from them what the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did in relation to praying for rain. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited with a state of humility and humility. The narrator has disagreed in quoting a single word here."
"1807","Hisham bin Ishaq narrates this statement of his father. An emir sent me to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) to ask him about the Istiqa prayer. Narrators named Harun and Yusuf narrated these words. So that I may inquire from him about the prayer to be recited in connection with the prayer for rain.' So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said, 'Why did he not inquire from me himself?' Prophet Muhammad did not give a sermon like you people."
"1808","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only raised his hands while praying for rain. These words are narrated along with another chain of transmission: Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never raised his hands while praying. He only raised his hands while praying for rain."
"1809","Salim narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in front of Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1810","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"1811","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “Do not declare your dead to be impure, because a Muslim is not impure in life or death.”"
"1812","Sayyiduna Abdullah Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Gabriel (A.S.) performed the funeral prayer for Sayyidna Adam (A.S.), he recited the takbirs for Sayyidna Adam. A tombstone was installed. The narrator of this tradition, Abd al-Rahman bin Malik, is obsolete."
"1813","Sayyidna Abi bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the angels had performed the funeral prayer of Sayyidna Adam (peace be upon him) and they had recited takbeers over him. They said: O children of Adam! This is your way (of performing the funeral prayer)."
"1814","This same hadith along with another chain of transmission is reported as a \suspended\"" hadith on the authority of Sayyiduna Abi (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"1815","This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Abi bin Ka'b (RA)."
"1816","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the angels said praises to Sayyidna Adam (peace be upon him), Sayyidna Abu Bakr said praises to the Prophet (peace be upon him), Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said praises to Sayyidna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) said praises to Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Imam Hasan (may God bless him and grant him peace) said praises to Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyidna Imam Hussain said four takbeers on Sayyidna Imam Hasan (RA)."
"1817","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) offered a funeral prayer."
"1818","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) recited four takbeers in the funeral prayer for the last time. Sayyiduna Imam Hussain (RA) recited four Takbirs in the funeral prayer of Sayyiduna Imam Hussain (RA) and the angels recited four Takbirs in the funeral prayer of Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him). The narrator of this hadith is Firat bin Sa'ib, this is an obsolete hadith."
"1819","Talha bin Abdullah narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) led a funeral prayer and he recited Surah Fatiha in it."
"1820","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when we give ghusl to the dead, one of us performs ghusl and the other does not (i.e. it is not necessary to perform ghusl after giving ghusl to the deceased)."
"1821","Ayyub bin Nu'man narrates that I performed a funeral prayer following the example of Sayyidna Zaid bin Arqam, and he recited five takbeers during it. The narrator quoted this hadith as a marfu' hadith."
